  "id": "Compound::DB00786 - Gene::9313",
  "verbalization": "Marimastat is likely to interact with Mmp20 through a shared pathway involving matrix metalloproteinases (MMPs). The evidence suggests that Marimastat binds to multiple MMPs, including Mmp23b, Mmp26, and Mmp27, which are all part of the MMP family and are involved in the degradation of extracellular matrix components. Since Mmp20 is listed as a participant in the pathway of these MMPs, it is plausible that Marimastat exerts its effects on Mmp20 through a mechanism involving the inhibition of MMPs. The high scores in the paths indicate a strong and consistent interaction, suggesting that Marimastat may act as a modulator of MMP activity, potentially influencing Mmp20 through the regulation of MMP expression or function. The mechanism is supported by the presence of multiple binding sites for Marimastat across different MMPs, reinforcing the hypothesis that it interacts with Mmp20 via a common pathway.",
